 "text": "Hello! How's everything today? Very normal, sadly. Our eyes are constantly checking for details, and screens never stop. It is a lot. One trick is to look at the horizon for a few minutes every hour or so. Look at the wall in front of you, or the cloud. Then try a dark room with a dim light at night. Your brain needs darkness to reset. They help, but only at night. During the day, get outside in the middle of the brightest light you can find, like at ridge top.",
